%global __debug_package	0
%global __strip	true

%global vmoddir	%{_libdir}/varnish/vmods
%global vcldir	%{_datadir}/varnish/vcl

Name:		@PACKAGE@
Version:	@PACKAGE_VERSION@
Release:	1%{?dist}
Summary:	JA4 TLS Client Fingerprinting VMOD for Varnish

License:	Unlicense
URL:		https://github.com/usdnag9ugudhi/libvmod-ja4
Source:		%{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildRequires:	pkgconfig(varnishapi) >= 9.1.0
BuildRequires:	openssl-devel

%description
Varnish VMOD that computes JA4 TLS Client Hello fingerprints from raw
wire bytes.

%prep
%setup -q

%build
%configure CFLAGS="%{optflags}" RST2MAN=:
%make_build V=1

%install
%make_install
rm -f %{buildroot}%{vmoddir}/*.la

%check
%make_build check

%files
%{_docdir}/%{name}/
%{_mandir}/man*/*
%{vmoddir}/libvmod_ja4.so

%changelog
* Thu Sep 24 2026 libvmod-ja4 maintainers - 1.1.0-1
- Require Varnish Cache 9.1.0; migrate the build to the VCACHE macros
  and vtest
- Fix a crash when the last VCL importing ja4 is discarded while TLS
  connections are open or handshaking (the rest of varnish/varnish#51):
  OpenSSL copies the msg callback into each connection, so link with
  -z nodelete and keep the vmod mapped; the discard event now only
  disarms it, so fingerprints also keep working when ja4 is imported
  again later
- Stop OpenSSL calling the msg callback for every record once the
  Client Hello phase is over
- Fix a race in the per-connection result cache when HTTP/2 streams on
  the same connection call ja4 concurrently, which could leak or use
  freed memory
- Serve cached results without locking: repeat calls on a connection
  now cost ~20 ns at any thread count, instead of contending on a
  global mutex (~14 us per call at 56 threads)
- Take the global mutex once per Client Hello instead of on every TLS
  message seen by the OpenSSL msg callback
- Simplify the code: keep cached results with the parsed Client Hello
  instead of a second ex_data index, drop stack-buffer scrubbing and
  unreachable clamps, and size scratch buffers from the parser limits

* Sat Sep 12 2026 libvmod-ja4 maintainers - 1.0.1-1
- Unregister OpenSSL callbacks on the last vcl.discard, fixing a
  crash after VCL reload (varnish/varnish#51)

* Sun Mar 22 2026 libvmod-ja4 maintainers - 1.0-1
- Release 1.0

* libvmod-ja4 maintainers - 0.1
- Initial package
